## arreo update verify — the user door, through the real binary (T-0036)

### 1. an artifact with no signature: exit 1, names what is missing

update: arreo-0.1.0-x86_64: no signature at arreo-0.1.0-x86_64.minisig — refusing an unverified artifact
exit=1

### 2. missing artifact argument: usage, exit 2

update: verify needs the path of the artifact to check
usage: arreo update verify <path> [--sig <path>] [--manifest <path>] [--json]
  <path>      the artifact to check; its signature is <path>.minisig
  --sig       the signature to use instead of the sibling <path>.minisig
  --manifest  a signed SHA256SUMS; verified first, then used to check the digest
  exit codes: 0 verified · 1 refused · 2 usage — there is no bypass flag
exit=2

### 3. --force: refused as an unknown flag (no bypass exists)

update: unknown flag --force
usage: arreo update verify <path> [--sig <path>] [--manifest <path>] [--json]
  <path>      the artifact to check; its signature is <path>.minisig
  --sig       the signature to use instead of the sibling <path>.minisig
  --manifest  a signed SHA256SUMS; verified first, then used to check the digest
  exit codes: 0 verified · 1 refused · 2 usage — there is no bypass flag
exit=2

### 4. a signature made by another key (fresh real minisign keypair): UnknownKeyId, exit 1

update: arreo-0.1.0-x86_64: signed by key AEC6DF2C25AFE72A, this build trusts 076F2F7CEBE0AF51
exit=1
